From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:41:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] Android: build Patchy as a Qt for Android app

A qt_add_executable target on Android (cmake/patchy_android.cmake) whose
fonts, translations and bundled scripts ride along as Qt resources, since
the executable directory is the read-only native-library folder. The web
build's metric-compatible fonts come too, without the CJK families Android
already has. Build-host steps that run the freshly built binary, the
plug-in and TLS file checks, test fixtures and the Linux install rules are
skipped. The desktop menu bar stays a menu bar instead of moving into the
Android options menu, and the web build's font stand-ins apply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
